From: hayaksi1 <193020925+hayaksi1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 20:03:28 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Restore the two closing lines a merge dropped from the
 desktop IPC tests

The merged file did not parse: an it() block opened at line 182 was never
closed, and describe("setThemeColor") began immediately after it, so oxfmt
could not format the file and oxlint reported "Expected } but found EOF".
Both source branches are individually valid - one carries the setThemeColor
tests, the others the displayMedia tests - and the resolution lost the two
lines that closed the test and its enclosing describe.

There were no conflict markers left behind, which is why the marker guard
passed it. Five setThemeColor tests and two displayMedia tests were sitting
inside a file no runner could load.

Fork-Feature: fork-tooling
---
 apps/desktop/src/ipc.test.ts | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/apps/desktop/src/ipc.test.ts b/apps/desktop/src/ipc.test.ts
index 2e749e533d..76a4c5b4a4 100644
--- a/apps/desktop/src/ipc.test.ts
+++ b/apps/desktop/src/ipc.test.ts
@@ -185,6 +185,8 @@ describe("ipcCall: callDisplayMediaCallback", () => {
         await callIpc("callDisplayMediaCallback", 14, [{}]);
 
         expect(send).toHaveBeenCalledWith("ipcReply", { id: 14, reply: null });
+    });
+});
 
 describe("setThemeColor", () => {
     let handler: (ev: unknown, color: unknown) => void;
-- 
